server localhost => accepted: hi
eku localhost => refused: tls: certificate is not for a server (its extended key usage does not include serverAuth)
nosan localhost => refused: tls: certificate has no subjectAltName (a Common Name alone is not accepted)
sha1 localhost => refused: tls: certificate 1 of the chain is signed with SHA-1, which is no longer accepted
ku localhost => refused: tls: the certificate's key usage does not allow it to be used for this connection
wild a.test.localhost => accepted: hi
wild A.TEST.localhost. => accepted: hi
wild a.b.test.localhost => refused: tls: certificate does not match host name "a.b.test.localhost"
wild test.localhost => refused: tls: certificate does not match host name "test.localhost"
wild x.localhost => refused: tls: certificate does not match host name "x.localhost"
wild example.com => refused: tls: certificate does not match host name "example.com"
ipsan 127.0.0.1 => accepted: hi
ipsan 127.0.0.2 => refused: tls: certificate does not match host name "127.0.0.2"
ipsan localhost => refused: tls: certificate does not match host name "localhost"
server 127.0.0.1 => refused: tls: certificate does not match host name "127.0.0.1"
ipsan by address => accepted: hi
[a.test.localhost\0.evil] => refused: tls: server name contains a NUL byte
[*.test.localhost] => refused: tls: server name contains '*' (a wildcard is a certificate's, not a host's)
[a..test.localhost] => refused: tls: server name has an empty label
[.localhost] => refused: tls: server name has an empty label
[bücher.localhost] => refused: tls: server name is not ASCII (use its IDNA xn-- form)
[a b.localhost] => refused: tls: server name contains a character no host name has
[localhost.] => refused: tls: certificate does not match host name "localhost."
[a.test.localhost..] => refused: tls: server name has an empty label
[-a.test.localhost] => refused: tls: server name has a label that starts with '-'
[a-.test.localhost] => refused: tls: server name has a label that ends with '-'
[a.test.localhost:443] => refused: tls: server name contains ':' but is not an IPv6 address
[[::1]] => refused: tls: server name contains ':' but is not an IPv6 address
